      "content": "It's completely understandable to feel that way when the routine is so soul-crushing; it feels like just existing to get through the hours. If the whole system feels pointless, focusing on grand changes is exhausting. Instead, maybe you could find one tiny thing that is *yours* during your shift, even if it's just a specific song you listen to or a particular quiet corner you find. These small pockets of autonomy can be a quiet rebellion against the feeling of being a replaceable part.",
      "source": "target",
